# valgrind suppressions for the swBroker functest suite (--vt).
#
# Scope: only genuinely-unavoidable noise from third-party libraries that the
# broker links but does not own (mongo C driver / libbson, OpenSSL, libpq,
# libmicrohttpd, glibc loader). Add an entry ONLY after confirming the stack is
# entirely in library code and not reachable from broker allocations.
#
# Generate candidates with:  valgrind ... --gen-suppressions=all
#
# glibc per-thread resolver state (resolv_conf) cached during a DNS lookup in
# the mongo C driver's background server-monitor thread. That thread is torn
# down at process exit before glibc frees its thread-local resolver config, so
# valgrind reports the cached config as lost. Entirely inside glibc/mongoc — not
# reachable from broker allocations.
{
   mongoc-server-monitor-getaddrinfo-resolv
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect
   ...
   fun:getaddrinfo
   ...
   fun:_server_monitor_thread
}

# Same glibc per-thread resolver state (resolv_conf), but cached during a DNS
# lookup the broker itself makes when downloading a remote @context
# (swldContextFromUrl -> connCreate -> getaddrinfo) on a REST worker thread.
# Worker threads are not joined at exit, so glibc never frees their thread-local
# resolver config. The lost block is glibc's resolv_conf, not a broker
# allocation.
{
   broker-context-download-getaddrinfo-resolv
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite,indirect
   ...
   fun:getaddrinfo
   ...
   fun:swRestWorkerMain
}
